|> Exercise
    handle=_no_solutions_by_complete_square_

    Show that
    $$
    x^2 + 10x + 30 = 0
    $$
    (cf$.$ Exercise >>_complete_square_1_) has no solutions $x \in \rr$.

    |> Solution

        The equation is equivalent to
        $$
        (x + 5)^2 + 5 = 0
        $$
        by Exercise >>_complete_square_1_, but this implies
        $$
        (x + 5)^2 = -5
        $$
        which is an equation with no solution over
        the reals because the square of a real number
        is nonnegative.
